  "title": "CHAPTER 4: HINDI GRAMMAR :VYAKARAN (व्याकरण)",
  "order": 4,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "ysg0ff5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.1 Devanagari Script :Varnamala (वर्णमाला)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Devanagari Script (Varnamala) forms the phonetic and structural foundation of Hindi grammar.",
        "Shabda Vichar covers word formation, etymology, and linguistic classification.",
        "Main parts of speech analyzed include Sangya (Noun), Sarvanam (Pronoun), Visheshan (Adjective), and Kriya (Verb) with Kaal (Tense).",
        "Sandhi (sound conjunctions) and Samas (compound words) govern complex word formation rules.",
        "Muhavare (Idioms) and Lokoktiyaan (Proverbs) are high-priority practical components for competitive examinations."
      ],
      "id": "qzxb7ru"
    },
